.TH ORIGIN-SECRETS 1 "2026" "Origin Secrets v0.4.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
origin-secrets \- threshold secrets management with post-quantum verification
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B origin-secrets
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIcommand-options\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B origin-secrets
splits a master secret into K-of-N shares using Reed-Solomon erasure coding.
Each share carries a hybrid Ed25519 + Falcon-1024 signature. Recovery requires
any K shares; fewer than K reveals nothing. The vault is encrypted with
XChaCha20-Poly1305 and an Argon2id-derived key.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-vault \fIPATH\fR
Vault file path (default: ~/.origin/secrets.vault; a leading ~ is expanded to
your home directory).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-passphrase-file \fIPATH\fR
File containing the vault passphrase. \fBRequired for every command\fR \(em
there is no built-in default, so a command without \-p fails with
.B PassphraseRequired
rather than silently using a weak key.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a structured JSON payload on stdout for success (and, on error, a JSON
envelope with code / severity / message). Without \fB\-\-json\fR, output is
human-readable.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite an existing target file (used by shard, export-share, recover
\-\-vault-out, and the audit compliance exports). By default an existing file is
refused.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init \-\-tier \fITIER\fR
Create an encrypted vault and derive a master seed. TIER is one of
nano, standard, sovereign.
.TP
.B shard \-\-key \fINAME\fR \-\-threshold \fIK\fR \-\-shares \fIN\fR [\-\-force]
Split the master key into N signed shares requiring any K to recover. Refuses to
overwrite a pre-existing shares/ directory unless \-\-force is given.
.TP
.B export-share \-\-share \fINUM\fR \-\-out \fIPATH\fR [\-\-recipient \fINAME\fR] [\-\-force]
Export share NUM as an encrypted, recipient-bound file. Refuses to overwrite
PATH unless \-\-force is given.
.TP
.B recover \fISHARE\fR... [\-o \fIOUT\fR] [\-\-vault-out \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-tier \fITIER\fR] [\-\-force]
Reconstruct the master seed from >= K shares. The recovered seed is written to
\-o or to the rebuilt vault at \-\-vault-out; in human mode it is never printed to
the terminal. \-\-vault-out refuses to overwrite unless \-\-force is given.
.TP
.B verify [\-\-vault-path \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-share \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-recovery-log]
Verify vault integrity, or a share's full hybrid signature (when the vault is
supplied). With \-\-recovery-log, confirms the vault carries at least one Recover
audit entry.
.TP
.B audit [\-\-show-recovery-log] [\-\-show-all-logs] [\-\-show-failures] [\-\-export-soc2 \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-export-pcidss \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-export-hipaa \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-force]
Show or export the audit/recovery log as compliance evidence. \-\-show-failures
reads the vault-independent failure journal; all display modes honor \-\-json.
Only one compliance export may be requested per invocation, and each refuses to
overwrite unless \-\-force is given.
.TP
.B completions \fISHELL\fR
Print a shell completion script for SHELL (one of bash, zsh, fish) to stdout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
Internal/runtime failure (crypto error, I/O error, vault corruption, tampering
detected).
.TP
2
Usage error (passphrase missing or too weak) \(em fix the invocation.
.TP
3
Not-found / input error (vault, share, or key missing; invalid threshold;
FileAlreadyExists when overwriting without \-\-force; StdoutSecretRefused when a
seed would be dumped to a terminal without \-o/--json).
.TP
127
CLI parse error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.EX
echo "correct horse battery staple" > ./pw.txt
origin-secrets -V ./vault -p ./pw.txt init --tier standard
origin-secrets -V ./vault -p ./pw.txt shard --key master --threshold 3 --shares 5
origin-secrets -V ./vault -p ./pw.txt recover shares/share_001.json \\
  shares/share_002.json shares/share_003.json -o seed.recovered
origin-secrets -V ./vault -p ./pw.txt audit --export-soc2 soc2.json
origin-secrets -p ./pw.txt audit --show-failures --json
origin-secrets completions bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/origin-secrets
.EE
